# STUB — Nuxel phone features patch for linux-postmarketos-exynos9820
#
# TODO: port the Nuxel drivers/nuxel patch (see patches/README.md and
# patches/0001-nuxel-phone-features.README for the full analysis).
#
# The original 0001-nuxel-phone-features.patch (the Pixel 10 Pro XL / Tensor
# G5 6.12 GKI tree, see kernel/google-pixel-10-pro-xl/patches/) is NOT copied
# here. Its C code is expected to compile on the exynos9820 tree (it uses
# struct proc_ops and saved_command_line, neither of which is 6.12-only), but
# its drivers/Kconfig and drivers/Makefile wiring hunks are context-dependent
# and it hardcodes nuxel.device=mustang. Until the port is verified against
# the cloned tree this file intentionally contains NO diff hunks, so
# `git apply` reports "No valid patches" rather than a silent success.
#
# Port checklist (see patches/README.md):
#   [ ] drivers/nuxel/Kconfig (NUXEL, NUXEL_PHONE, NUXEL_BOOT_PARAM)
#   [ ] drivers/nuxel/Makefile (nuxel-core.o when CONFIG_NUXEL=y)
#   [ ] drivers/nuxel/nuxel-core.c (nuxel.boot=1 / nuxel.device=s10plus)
#   [ ] drivers/Kconfig: source "drivers/nuxel/Kconfig"
#   [ ] drivers/Makefile: obj-$(CONFIG_NUXEL) += nuxel/
#   [ ] git -C kernel/s10plus/.build/src apply --check \
#       kernel/s10plus/patches/0001-nuxel-phone-features.patch  (must pass)
#   [ ] kernel/s10plus/defconfig: uncomment CONFIG_NUXEL / CONFIG_NUXEL_PHONE /
#       CONFIG_NUXEL_BOOT_PARAM once the port compiles
